      "content": "hey, i work in architecture and i've been staying in this new smart-complex downtown lately. i'm noticing something really weird with the HVAC and the LED lighting cycles. there's this constant, almost imperceptible thrumming/flicker that doesn't match the standard mechanical specs for buildings this size. it's like it's pulsing at a very specific low frequency. has anyone ever documented HVAC systems being used to modulate ambient resonance for mood control or something? it's making me feel incredibly on edge.",
